Tom Biedermann notes on helping me learn how to write succinct emails! So kind and helpful!
"As a fellow long-email enjoyer: no worries 🙂
If useful, my learnings from working with execs who want 3-dotpoint emails (but also should really be across the context): 

    BLUF: Bottom Line Up Front - put the key info / ask / call for action of your email in the first sentence or 2. Don't bury the lede. Provide the conclusion, not the argument. Imagine that is all they will read. Does your email stand up? 

    Keep the context / example / arguments in but clearly separated: separate paragraphs and/or a mini heading. If they want to read, they can but again, imagine that they won't (i.e. you never get to invoke "this was in the Nth paragraph of my email!", for N>=2 😄).


Hope this helps. "

