I was in such terrible grid lock that I could not bring myself to do my work.
In particular the fear of failure and perfectionism was so crippling there was one night where I spent about 6 hours rewriting one line of an introduction. 
Absolute killer! 

Then I started watching psychotherapeautic videos about perfectionism and fear of failure.
I learned the phrase:
" The opposite of perfectionism is the attunement to reality."
This phrase was like a lightning bolt and made perfect logical sense to me. 
I was not accepting failure by not doing something perfectly. 
I was accepting that REALISTICALLY I can only achieve so much and perfection is illogical! Nor realistic!

It unstuck me and I was able to make mistakes. 
I also want to make note here Dabrowski's theory of Positive Disintigration.
Though not perfect, it has really made sense for me in the therapeautic journey of understanding having a 2e AuDHD brain. 
Sometimes simple things are incredibly complex and hard for me but when I am provided with the right information, I am very good at applying it immediately and growing rapidly!!

In this same way, 
I found the first semester a huge struggle. 
None of the systems of organisation, study, motivation, focus etc. that I have found recommended work for me. 

The reality of having a PDA (pervasive drive for autonomy) profile with AuDHD and 2e, is that the conditions I need to meet to have sustainable productive work are not typical nor do I find much information online to be of any help whatsoever. 
If you have ever heard the phrase 'If you have met one person with autism, you have met one person with autism'.

I self-devised a system for studying over the holiday break while in autistic burn out that has really worked for me.
It might seem a little strange to other people but it really works for me!

